# .slugignore — paths Heroku strips from the compiled slug at build time.
# Same matching as .gitignore, EXCEPT there is no negation: you cannot write
# `tests` here and re-include `tests/foo.html`. Exclude whole directories only.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-08-05)
# server.js mounts a lot of the repo as PUBLIC static directories. `tests` was
# one of them (`app.use('/tests', express.static(...))`, no gate), so every
# file committed under tests/ was published to the open web. A unit-test
# fixture for the staff-only contract-embroidery margin overlay hardcoded the
# real production cost model, and `curl https://…/tests/unit/dst-quote-math.test.js`
# returned it 200/no-auth — defeating the requireStaff endpoint it was testing.
# CLAUDE.md rule 2 requires ALL tests live in /tests, so keeping them out of
# the slug is what stops that recurring for the next fixture.
#
# Verified safe before adding (2026-08-05):
#   · scripts/build.js (heroku-postbuild + prestart) has zero tests/ references
#   · nothing in the app links to /tests/ (no href/src anywhere outside tests/)
#   · the three sendFile routes at server.js:7096-7108 point at files that were
#     already deleted and already 404 in production
#
# ⚠️ NOT a substitute for removing the mount. If this file is ever deleted the
# directory becomes public again — the durable fix is dropping the `/tests`
# static mount in server.js.
#
# ⚠️ `scripts` canNOT be added here: heroku-postbuild runs `node scripts/build.js`,
# so excluding it breaks the build. It is also publicly mounted — close that one
# by removing its static mount, not here.
tests
